            <div xml:id="d30-a1">

                <pb facs="0140" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg52"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 284.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Señor Errazuriz.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-24"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to refer to my notes of 30th
                    September and of 13th December, 1890, addressed to the ministry of your
                    excellency with regard to certain claims of citizens of the United States
                    against your excellency’s Government, and to say that I was informed by Señor
                    don Domingo Godoy, minister of foreign relations, at the end of December, 1890,
                    that the various documents which accompanied my note of 13th December had been
                    placed in the hands of the honorable fiscal of the supreme court, Señor don
                    Ambrosio Montt, for his examination and opinion. May I ask your excellency to
                    kindly inform me what progress has been made in said examination?</p>
                <p>I shall proceed, without delay, to arrange and forward to your excellency the
                    documents in support of the list of claims arising out of the war between Chile
                    and Peru, referred to in my note of 30th September, 1890, as also some small
                    claims arising out of the late war, and I beg to convey the assurance of my
                    earnest desire to cooperate with your excellency in the thorough investigation
                    of these several claims and in bringing them to a settlement that will be
                    mutually satisfactory to our respective Governments.</p>
                <p>Renewing, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Patrick Egan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
